{"event_type":"review","id":"defc757f76531bfc6f60e5a6365ec71bef2472e69aab80b264615a193b8041aa","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T20:53:59Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7ab140783d32f52ccdb52bc9fa5ba4583d2b62a94584300edcd8420e2b471dd8","sha256":"7ab140783d32f52ccdb52bc9fa5ba4583d2b62a94584300edcd8420e2b471dd8"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/569cb8c0c4fd7e236bb52e2eaaa9cab4f177afc070c758b4bd3f72d745ed5631","sha256":"569cb8c0c4fd7e236bb52e2eaaa9cab4f177afc070c758b4bd3f72d745ed5631"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3480f3af3a248d8d28e2ca6dc3df6292ac1653fbce948bef7f8e07d85eed329c","sha256":"3480f3af3a248d8d28e2ca6dc3df6292ac1653fbce948bef7f8e07d85eed329c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/507ade272b48c9b5a608713083ab137bad74e370a764087dac7fb87732866371","sha256":"507ade272b48c9b5a608713083ab137bad74e370a764087dac7fb87732866371"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/68f20c545eba80968c914e75759378c605f03018c9025d0fd7a2810ee74b4eba","sha256":"68f20c545eba80968c914e75759378c605f03018c9025d0fd7a2810ee74b4eba"}],"attempt_id":"54214f9d07d2c8f4ddeb934f0b676f5c0d03505a75518cff939503b33622ad88:0:1","base":"ebed88ca0245e0b3764ca53586b2a11d101f4819","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7e4249992da59bb1a17670281e6e4b1973b5cef6","body":"**Skip unscannable prior-attempt feedback instead of aborting the rescue.**\n\n`failedAttemptFeedback` throws when the prior attempt touched certain files (`failedAttemptContents`, taskLoop.ts:1255-1266):\n- a binary file;\n- a file larger than 4 MiB;\n- a file that contains U+FFFD.\n\nThe throw happens before `invoke`, so the rescue tier fails without running the model. The catch then records another failed attempt with gate `none`, and the configured escalation step is spent.\n\nFeedback is optional context. When feedback cannot be scanned safely, leave it out and still run the rescue with the plain prompt. The prompt already handles `priorFailedFeedback === undefined`. The scanner guarantee stays intact because nothing unscanned is uploaded.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if (decision.tier === 'rescue' && priorRound?.failedAttempt !== undefined) {\n-          priorFailedFeedback = await failedAttemptFeedback(git, priorRound.failedAttempt);\n+          try {\n+            priorFailedFeedback = await failedAttemptFeedback(git, priorRound.failedAttempt);\n+          } catch {\n+            // Unscannable or moved prior attempt: rescue proceeds without the patch.\n+            priorFailedFeedback = undefined;\n+          }\n         }\n```\nIf a ref mismatch must stay fatal, rethrow only the branch-ref and parentage errors.\n</details>","id":"14362e53b0b2af43654af19158503b5b3e7950717a55065a31c06d6eba375b8d","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/sweep/taskLoop.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Skip unscannable prior-attempt feedback instead of aborting the rescue."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7e4249992da59bb1a17670281e6e4b1973b5cef6","body":"**Do not create failed-attempt commits when the attempt changed nothing.**\n\nSeveral failures throw before the worker writes any bytes:\n- the budget is exhausted at `invoke` start (taskLoop.ts:505-514);\n- the scanner refuses the upload (taskLoop.ts:479-488);\n- `failedAttemptFeedback` throws (taskLoop.ts:430).\n\nIn each case, `recordFailedAttempt` still runs `git add -A`, writes the unchanged tree, and pins a commit under `<runPrefix>/failed/...`.\n\nWhen `pushFailed` and `publishFailedAttempts` are both set, the scan passes trivially at taskLoop.ts:1023-1058. The empty branch is then pushed to `origin`. runFix then reports the row with `branch`/`sha` and renders a compare link to an empty diff. The row should be a branchless no-artifact failure instead.\n\nThe call sites already expect an optional result. taskLoop.ts:857 and taskLoop.ts:998 both use `row.failedAttempt === undefined ? {} : …`. The helper never returns `undefined`.\n\nTo fix this, check `git diff --cached --quiet <parent>` after staging. If nothing is staged, return `undefined`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      ): Promise<FailedAttempt> => {\n+      ): Promise<FailedAttempt | undefined> => {\n         if (parent === undefined) throw new Error('failed attempt has no pre-attempt HEAD');\n         const kind = bindings.segments?.kind ?? unit.fixer;\n         const slug = bindings.segments?.slug ?? unit.package;\n         await git(['add', '-A', '--', '.']);\n+        const staged = await git(['diff', '--cached', ...SWEEP_DIFF_FLAGS, '--name-only', '-z', parent, '--']);\n+        if (staged === '') return undefined;\n         const failedAttempt = await commitFailedAttempt(git, {\n```\nAlso change the assignments at taskLoop.ts:851 and taskLoop.ts:992 so that they delete `row.failedAttempt` when the helper returns `undefined`.\n</details>","id":"4a4b1525a64c9ca86549d74b8137d3c1e4b90f54ea04d756acfa52f6a7bd5d7b","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/sweep/taskLoop.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not create failed-attempt commits when the attempt changed nothing."}],"head":"6294758590c8a2281a8f888c492dd739b6d7d6a0","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"8acf0b45fc14797b7fa45baa7b3aa5f585dc1d5b","intervals":[[7,7],[53,77],[103,106],[193,197],[199,200],[203,203]],"path":"docs/ops/fix.run.md"},{"blob":"403c075d4a9456cea3bbb35243d68bf79020482a","intervals":[[8,9],[11,32],[52,52],[57,57],[63,63],[65,77],[81,87],[94,109],[113,120],[132,320],[334,334],[341,351],[358,400],[402,439],[447,482],[495,503],[525,616],[618,618],[636,637],[662,662],[703,710],[736,747],[757,757],[768,768